# Changelog

All notable changes to Monochrome will be documented here.

Format: [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/)  
Versioning: [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html)

---

## [Unreleased]

---

## [1.0.1] — 2026

### Added
- Regex validation for track, artist, and album IDs before constructing Discord presence URLs, based on Wikidata format constraints (P4578, P4576, P4577)

### Changed
- Album art in Discord Rich Presence is now built from the TIDAL CDN using the album cover UUID instead of scraping an `<img>` element from the DOM
- Local file tracks now read TIDAL metadata (cover art, IDs, URLs) from a `tidalData` field on the track object, so Discord Rich Presence works correctly for locally matched tracks
- `build_activity` and `update_discord_presence` in `desktop.rs` now take `ActivityParams` and `PresencePayload` structs instead of individual arguments

---

## [1.0.0] — 2026

### Added
- Initial release of Monochrome desktop client for Windows
- Tauri v2 wrapper for [monochrome.tf](https://monochrome.tf) with WebView2
- Discord Rich Presence — track title, artist, album art, playback timestamps, and clickable URLs
- Media key support (play/pause via `MediaPlayPause` global shortcut)
- System tray with show/hide, set download folder, and quit actions
- Desktop notifications for track changes when the window is unfocused
- Single-instance enforcement — re-focuses existing window on relaunch
- Custom source URL fallback screen for self-hosted or local dev instances
- Persistent download folder preference saved to app config directory
- Persistent window size and position via `tauri-plugin-window-state`
- Google OAuth via `tauri-plugin-google-auth`
- External link router — opens `_blank` and off-origin links in the system browser
- Windows installer bundles: `.msi` (WiX) and `.exe` (NSIS)
- GitHub Actions CI workflow for automated Windows builds and draft releases